\ Mutable-map construction, in-place mutation, and access compile to direct
\ native calls under interpreter-free AOT with the interpreter setting locked
\ off. Building previously failed because `make-mutable-map`, `@set!`, and
\ `@get` each emitted a `jitNativeWordCall` fallback, which the zero-fallback
\ class rejects; a clean build and exit prove the direct-call codegen carries
\ no fallback. `make-vector` is exercised the same way. No printing or
\ arithmetic on the results, so the binary links no interpreter. Result
\ correctness is checked separately under runtime-image AOT, where output can
\ be printed.
M{ } "k" 1 @set! "k" @get drop

